@@ -0,0 +1,672 @@
+//! Operator-configured internal MCP gateway.
+//!
+//! Mirrors [`crate::nearai_mcp`] — an env-configured hosted MCP provider that
+//! composition registers in the extension catalog and auto-enables on boot —
+//! with three differences:
+//!
+//! - the endpoint URL is taken verbatim (path included), because the gateway
+//!   serves JSON-RPC on `/mcp/post` rather than the `/mcp` NEAR AI expects;
+//! - private address ranges are allowed, because the gateway is a service on
+//!   the operator's own Docker network (see [`crate::mcp`] for the single
+//!   egress-policy branch that permits it);
+//! - activation runs hosted MCP discovery instead of the static path, so the
+//!   aggregated backends' tools are published without being enumerated in the
+//!   bundled manifest.
+//!
+//! The extension only exists when `CLAWBOT_MCP_GATEWAY_URL` is set. Without it
+//! composition never builds the package, so nothing downstream can reach a
+//! private target through this provider.
